{c: Chords: the writer's own chart}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Saved from [C2]death, saved from [G]Hell, saved from [D]sin
One day [Em]saved from the [Cmaj7]troubles I’m [D]in
Saved to [C2]serve, saved to [G]love, saved to [D]give
Saved to [Em]follow the [Cmaj7]Christ, saved to [D]live
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Interlude}
[Em]Hallelujah, [C]hallelujah, [Am]hallelu[D]jah [B]
[Em]Hallelujah, [C]hallelujah, [Am]hallelu[D]jah [B]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
I am [Em]saved, yes I’m [C]saved, I am [G]saved [D] [B]
I am [Em]saved, yes I’m [C]saved, I am [G]sav[D]ed
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Saved from enemies dragging me down
He saved me for honour and a crown
Saved to know deepest peace, saved to see
Saved to be everything I should be
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Interlude}
[Em]Hallelujah, [C]hallelujah, [Am]hallelu[D]jah [B]
[Em]Hallelujah, [C]hallelujah, [Am]hallelu[D]jah [B]
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Saved to know satisfaction and joy
That no-one can steal or destroy
Though each day may bring tears till I die
One day He’ll wipe every tear from my eye
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Interlude}
[Em]Hallelujah, [C]hallelujah, [Am]hallelu[D]jah [B]
[Em]Hallelujah, [C]hallelujah, [Am]hallelu[D]jah [B]
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
